   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 Ripple\n\nEdit **two frames** of a shot in any image editor; H3 carries the edit through every frame of the shot.\n\n1. **Ripple Clip** — upload a video. Drag the **blue window** (the frames H3 generates) to the shot you want.\n   Move the two **numbered markers** to frames where the subject is clearly visible.\n2. On each card, **Download frame**, make the **same change** in both images (keep the size), then\n   **upload**, **drop** the file on the card, or select the node and **Ctrl+V** a copied image.\n3. **Run.** Ripple Output saves `ripple/edit_*.mp4` (with the source audio) and `ripple/edit_compare_*.mp4`\n   (source | result, yellow bar = edited frame).\n\nChanging only the edits re-uses the decoded clip, the encoded prompt and the encoded source,\nso a re-run goes almost straight to sampling.\n\n**Keyboard** (node selected): ← / → step the selected marker · Shift+← / → move the window · Tab next marker.\n\n**In-graph editing:** connect *frames_to_edit* to an editor and its output to *edited_images* on Ripple Apply\n(one image per marker, in time order). Connected images override uploaded edits.\n\n### What H3_Ripple_v1 was trained on\n- FL2VA base + this LoRA at strength 1, the fixed prompt on Ripple Apply (leave it), CFG 1.\n- Two edited frames per shot. One works less reliably; three or four are experimental.\n- 384p up to 107 frames (4.46 s) · 352p up to 124 · 544p up to 56. The node warns outside these.\n- 24 fps. Other frame rates are resampled; some native frames can't be picked.\n\nThe **8-step accelerator** loader is bypassed: enable it (Ctrl+B) and set steps to 8 to try faster renders.\nIt has not been tested together with Ripple.\n"
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
